{"parentUuid":"e92e4464-76f7-421d-9a5d-400ecc1d9748","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgygLbGebCYNLwBnmpdwY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"S3 is committed as 2fc4f28 and not pushed.\n\nYou choose servers with the same top-bar switcher as before (All servers · local · two). I added no new selector. The switcher now also offers All servers on Workspaces, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions. On All servers, each server gets its own section, and the \"local\" and \"two\" names are only headings for those sections. The switcher sits at the top right of the bar today. Tell me if you want it moved to the left.\n\n**S3 summary:**\n- **Workspaces:** I tested this in the app. Each server has its section. Edit in the \"two\" section filled only the \"two\" form, so messages and changes go to that section's server.\n- **Rules tabs:** Each server has its section, and changes go through a context that points at that server.\n- **Steps tab:** It still shows one server, because a canvas edits one workflow.\n- **Checks:** CI and the safeguard pass.\n\n**One check I couldn't finish:** Server \"two\" (pid 32561, port 49191) runs a build too old to have scopes. Its constraints have no `steps` field, so a scope change can't land there, and I couldn't confirm a rules change in its section. It also shows every item as Off. Restart it on the new build and it will run migrations up to 10. I don't know how it was started, so I left it alone.\n\n**Remaining:** S4, charter edits committed to a new branch. Only 1.2Gi of disk is free again, and this round of builds used about 3Gi. Free more space before S4."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":377969,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":486,"cache_read_input_tokens":377969,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2fbe65a8-7db1-4fd3-873e-2428f8c7dcb7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgygLawYw8kPkZkhAdQn7","type":"assistant","uuid":"5df5a05c-ad58-4ff6-a958-6ccf75d858af","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:39:06.336Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
